The official bare run ended `budget_bound`: every rung through `p=4049` was solved by at least one vendor, while the generator could still enlarge a four-integer answer. That candidate is therefore parked, not falsely rejected. Before stopping, I’m testing the paper’s other native object—the original edge-triangle packing problem—with randomly decomposable graphs, to see whether it supplies a genuine Track‑A family rather than the transparent crown-matching subclass.
